[D Quests for Dire Maul West \\ https://github.com/JanRK/Guidelime_DungeonQuests]
[N 55-60 Dire Maul West]
[NX 57-60 Lower Blackrock Spire]

Dire Maul West is entered from the courtyard inside the ruins of Eldre'Thalas, through the main gate on its south side. Its door needs the Crescent Key, which Pusillin drops in Dire Maul East; do that wing first. Inside, the Shen'dralar Ancient sends you against Immol'thar, and the Athenaeum at the end of the wing holds the reward chest and the lorekeepers.

-- Left out: 7462 The Treasure of the Shen'dralar (Alliance copy): Questie blacklists it as a duplicate of 7877, which QuestieDB opens to all races.
-- Left out: 1318 Unfinished Gordok Business: Questie blacklists it as a duplicate of 7703; 7703, 5528, 5519, 7429, 1193 (Gordok quests) belong to the Dire Maul North guide.
-- Left out: 7483 to 7485 (Libram quests, Lorekeeper Lydros): each needs a libram that drops at random plus Pristine Black Diamond, Large Brilliant Shards and Blood of Heroes; a crafting turn-in, not a dungeon-run quest (judgement).
-- Left out: 7463 Arcane Refreshment (Mage, level 60): its kill is Hydrospawn in Dire Maul East; see that guide's note.
-- Left out: 7507, 7508 (Nostro's Compendium, The Forging of Quel'Serrar): Questie blacklists both; 7509 continues in Onyxia's Lair.
-- Left out: 7643 Ancient Equine Spirit (Paladin) and 7631 Dreadsteed of Xoroth (Warlock): class-mount chains of 7 and 10 quests that start in Stormwind and the Burning Steppes.
-- Left out: 5247 Fragments of the Past and 5250 Starfall (Alliance): Kel'Theril chain from Winterspring and Eastern Plaguelands; Dire Maul only supplies a Vial of Dire Water.
-- Left out: 8948 to 8950, 8967, 8990, 8970, 8996, 9015 (dungeon-set upgrade chains), which only pass through Dire Maul.

-- Horde: Camp Mojache, Sage Korolusk.
[A Horde] Start at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens [G44.5,59.1 The Barrens] [OC] \\ The route walks from here.
[A Horde] South on the road to the top of the Great Lift [G45.5,66.0 The Barrens][G44.7,78.2 The Barrens][G45.0,90.0 The Barrens] [OC] \\ Elite Razorfen Battleguards, Thornweavers and Death's Head Cultists (level 33-34) are close to the east of the lift. Also elite Ambassador Malcin (36), Azzere the Skyblade (25), Hagg Taurenbane (26) and Razorfen Servitors (23-24); hostile quilboars, Kolkar centaurs, hyenas, thunderhawks, Owatanka, Hirzek, Kuz and Nak (13-27) along the road.
[A Horde] Ride the Great Lift down into Thousand Needles [G32.1,24.2 Thousand Needles] [OC]
[A Horde] Follow the canyon west into Feralas [G30.7,24.4 Thousand Needles][G21.2,23.4 Thousand Needles][G18.5,22.3 Thousand Needles][G15.7,22.3 Thousand Needles][G13.0,21.5 Thousand Needles][G10.3,21.5 Thousand Needles] [OC] \\ An Enraged Panther and Rok'Alim the Pounder (elite, level 30) may be on the way. Ravaging Tempest (elite, 40) roams near the lift; Galak centaurs, Gravelsnout kobolds, Crag Stalkers, cougars, Boulderkin and cloud serpents (25-30) line the canyon, and Tobin Wheeldon (40).
[A Horde] West past Thalanaar (Alliance; keep south of its guards) and on to Camp Mojache [G87.0,48.5 Feralas][G81,46 Feralas][G78.5,45.0 Feralas][G77.2,43.3 Feralas][G75.95,43.55 Feralas][G75.6,43.65 Feralas][G75.5,44.4 Feralas] [OC]
[A Horde] At Shyn, get the Camp Mojache flight path [P Camp Mojache] [G75.5,44.4 Feralas]
[A Horde] Sage Korolusk gives [QA7481 Elven Legends] [G74.4,44.0 Feralas]
[A Horde] North out of camp, over the hill past the pavilion and round the east side of the ruins to their south road [G75.6,43.65 Feralas][G75.95,43.55 Feralas][G76.2,43.8 Feralas][G76.2,41.2 Feralas][G76.9,37.4 Feralas][G75.2,35.2 Feralas][G73.4,33.9 Feralas][G70.0,37.3 Feralas][G66.5,41.3 Feralas][G63.8,44.7 Feralas] [OC] \\ Namida Grimtotem (elite, level 43) camps near 68,39; Gordok Ogre-Mages and Enforcers (elite, level 52-54) walk the road along the south wall. Gordunni ogres, Grimtotem tauren and Woodpaw gnolls (40-44) also lie on this loop.
[A Horde] West along the wall to the main gate of the ruins [G59.0,45.0 Feralas][G57.3,45.0 Feralas][G55.6,45.0 Feralas][G54.1,44.0 Feralas] [OC]

-- Alliance: Feathermoon Stronghold, Scholar Runethorn.
[A Alliance] Start in Ironforge at the Great Forge [G55.9,47.9 Ironforge] [OC] \\ The route walks to Menethil Harbor in the next steps. QuestieDB lists an Incubus (20-30) here; a warlock summon, not a road threat (judgement).
[A Alliance] Out of Ironforge and down to the Dun Morogh road, then east to the North Gate Pass [G53.6,33.9 Dun Morogh][G51.6,39.8 Dun Morogh][G56.9,47.1 Dun Morogh][G62.6,54.7 Dun Morogh][G67.0,52.5 Dun Morogh][G76.0,48.5 Dun Morogh][G81.5,41.0 Dun Morogh][G84.1,33.8 Dun Morogh] [OC] \\ QuestieDB places a Plague Zombie (level 50) near the road. Ghostfang and Hammerspine (elite, 10-12), Rockjaw troggs, leopards, bears and ice elementals (7-10) are near the road.
[A Alliance] Through the pass and north to Dun Algaz [G20.7,17.5 Loch Modan][G26.3,22.5 Loch Modan][G25.5,11.5 Loch Modan] [OC] \\ Elder Black Bears and Forest Lurkers (10-12).
[A Alliance] North into the Wetlands and west along the road to Menethil Harbor [G55.1,73.7 Wetlands][G57.0,49.5 Wetlands][G49.5,40.0 Wetlands][G35.0,40.5 Wetlands][G26.3,40.5 Wetlands][G23.4,42.5 Wetlands][G22.4,44.0 Wetlands][G14.0,47.0 Wetlands][G12.3,52.2 Wetlands] [OC] \\ Elite Dragonmaw orcs, Highland Lurkers and Elder Crocolisks (level 27-30) and Modr and Golm (elite, level 32) are near the road; all are far below your level. Also Goaz Warder, Nightveiled Rotheap and Highland Horror (elite, 28-32), and Mosshide gnolls, raptors, spiders, crocolisks, slimes and fen creatures (20-28).
[A Alliance] Through the town to the south pier [G9.5,59.7 Wetlands][G4.7,63.8 Wetlands] [OC] \\ Dwyer (46) is listed near the docks.
[A Alliance] Take the boat to Theramore [G4.7,63.8 Wetlands]
[A Alliance] Off the pier and get the Theramore flight path if you lack it [P Theramore] [G67.5,51.2 Dustwallow Marsh]
[A Alliance] North out of Theramore along the shore road into the Barrens [G66.8,48.0 Dustwallow Marsh][G64.5,44.6 Dustwallow Marsh][G64.0,41.0 Dustwallow Marsh][G63.0,38.0 Dustwallow Marsh][G61.9,32.5 Dustwallow Marsh][G61.3,27.0 Dustwallow Marsh][G57.2,20.8 Dustwallow Marsh][G55.7,17.4 Dustwallow Marsh][G55.0,16.5 Dustwallow Marsh][G54.3,15.2 Dustwallow Marsh][G54.3,13.9 Dustwallow Marsh][G53.5,10.7 Dustwallow Marsh][G62.8,53.6 The Barrens] [OC] \\ QuestieDB lists Sully McCleary (level 50, hostile) near the road north of Theramore. Also Mirefin murlocs, Darkfang Venomspitters and Noxious Flayers (35-38), Doctor Nimer (22), Guard Jameson (40) and the Haggard-Looking Man (48).
[A Alliance] West across the Barrens to the south road, then south to the top of the Great Lift [G52.0,43.8 The Barrens][G50.4,49.8 The Barrens][G47.5,58.0 The Barrens][G45.5,66.0 The Barrens][G44.7,78.2 The Barrens][G45.0,90.0 The Barrens] [OC] \\ Northwatch Hold (Alliance) is to the east; Camp Taurajo (Horde) is off the road to the west near 44,59, keep clear of its guards. Elite Razorfen quilboars (33-34) are near the lift. Also elite Ambassador Malcin (36), Azzere the Skyblade (25), Hagg Taurenbane (26), Razorfen Servitors (23-24); Kolkar, Bristleback, Razormane, hyenas and Owatanka (13-27).
[A Alliance] Ride the Great Lift down into Thousand Needles [G32.1,24.2 Thousand Needles] [OC]
[A Alliance] Follow the canyon west to Thalanaar [G30.7,24.4 Thousand Needles][G21.2,23.4 Thousand Needles][G18.5,22.3 Thousand Needles][G15.7,22.3 Thousand Needles][G13.0,21.5 Thousand Needles][G10.3,21.5 Thousand Needles][G89.5,45.9 Feralas] [OC] \\ An Enraged Panther and Rok'Alim the Pounder (elite, level 30) may be on the way. Ravaging Tempest (elite, 40) near the lift; Galak, Gravelsnout, Crag Stalkers, Boulderkin and serpents (25-30); Tobin Wheeldon (40).
[A Alliance] At Thalanaar, get the flight path [P Thalanaar] [G89.5,45.9 Feralas]
[A Alliance] West along the south road past Camp Mojache and Dire Maul to the coast pier [G81,46 Feralas][G79.4,50.9 Feralas][G77,52 Feralas][G70,51 Feralas][G63,49 Feralas][G61.5,47.5 Feralas][G55.1,44.7 Feralas][G50.0,43.7 Feralas][G44.8,43.0 Feralas][G43.1,42.8 Feralas] [OC] \\ Camp Mojache (Horde) lies just north of 79,46; Gordok ogres (elite, 52-54) walk the road by the ruins; a Vale Screamer (level 60) is near the pier. Also Woodpaw gnolls, Longtooth wolves, Groddoc Apes, diseased Forest Walkers, Fel Interlopers, Rogue Vale Screechers, Ironfur Bears, Simmering Elementals (40-48), Gordok Hyenas (52-53) and Mirrorscale (48) near 48,44.
[A Alliance] Take the boat to Feathermoon Stronghold [G43.1,42.8 Feralas]
[A Alliance] Off the pier and south to Fyldren Moonfeather; get the Feathermoon flight path [P Feathermoon] [G31.0,39.5 Feralas][G31.0,42.2 Feralas][G30.2,43.3 Feralas] \\ QuestieDB lists a hostile level 60 Altruist Ward near the inn; read it as a scripted marker, not a mob (judgement, unverified).
[A Alliance] Scholar Runethorn gives [QA7482 Elven Legends] [G31.6,43.5 Feralas]
[A Alliance] North to the pier [G31.0,42.2 Feralas][G31.0,39.5 Feralas] [OC]
[A Alliance] Board the boat back to the mainland [G31.0,39.5 Feralas] \\ Stay on until it docks on the Feralas coast.
[A Alliance] Off the pier and east along the road to the main gate of the ruins [G43.1,42.8 Feralas][G44.8,43.0 Feralas][G55.1,44.7 Feralas][G54.1,44.0 Feralas] [OC] \\ A Vale Screamer (level 60) near the coast pier; Gordok Ogre-Mages and Enforcers (elite, level 52-54) walk this road.

-- Both.
Through the main gate, then north over the open ground west of the inner walls to the West wing door in their west face [G55.5,42.1 Feralas][G55.8,36.9 Feralas][G57.5,34.3 Feralas][G60.3,30.2 Feralas] [OC] \\ You need the Crescent Key from Pusillin (Dire Maul East). Gordok ogres (elite) guard the courtyard. A Gordok Mauler (elite, 53-54) stands near the West door.

-- Inside.
The Shen'dralar Ancient near the start gives [QA7461 The Madness Within]
Kill the guardians of the five pylons, then Immol'thar [QC7461]
The Shen'dralar Ancient takes [QT7461 The Madness Within] and gives [QA7877 The Treasure of the Shen'dralar]
In the Athenaeum, after Prince Tortheldrin, use the Skeletal Remains of Telmius Dreamseeker beside Lorekeeper Lydros [QC7481][QC7482] \\ Dungeon Journal places Lydros in Dire Maul West.
Open the Treasure of the Shen'dralar in the Athenaeum [QT7877 The Treasure of the Shen'dralar]
If a class book dropped in any wing, loot starts its quest; turn it in to the lorekeepers in the Athenaeum [QA7498][QA7499][QA7500][QA7501][QA7502][QA7503][QA7504][QA7505][QA7506] [O]
Lorekeeper Kildrath takes [QT7498][QT7499][QT7500]; Lorekeeper Mykos takes [QT7501][QT7502][QT7503]; Lorekeeper Javon takes [QT7504][QT7505][QT7506]
Leave the dungeon [G60.3,30.2 Feralas] [OC]

